{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/crutkas/msys2-woarm64-build/pulls/14","id":4502436590,"node_id":"PR_kwDOT3jXJs8AAAABDF267g","html_url":"https://github.com/crutkas/msys2-woarm64-build/pull/14","diff_url":"https://github.com/crutkas/msys2-woarm64-build/pull/14.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/crutkas/msys2-woarm64-build/pull/14.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/crutkas/msys2-woarm64-build/issues/14","number":14,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add receipt-bound native ARM64 Git Bash MVP assembly and replay tooling","user":{"login":"crutkas","id":1462282,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NjIyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1462282?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas","html_url":"https://github.com/crutkas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":true},"body":"## Scope\n\nAdds native-only runtime assembly from exact package receipts, raw PE/import auditing, deterministic archive recreation, fresh moved-extraction replay, live native entrypoint/module attestation, and real encrypted SSH/verified HTTPS controls. Runtime, Git, OpenSSL, curl and admitted dependencies are consumed rather than rebuilt.\n\n**The requested named MVP ZIP is still gated, not released or claimed complete.** This draft PR contains the persisted implementation and measured progression.\n\n## Measured progression\n\n| Stage | Result | Boundary |\n|---|---|---|\n| Initial diagnostic root | 12,376 files / 333 ARM64 PEs; static DLL closure resolves | Non-admitted diagnostic projection |\n| First behavior replay | Ten cases pass; missing selected sed blocks submodules | Failure preserved |\n| Second behavior replay | Recursive submodules pass; relative CA path blocks HTTPS | No TLS verification bypass |\n| Corrected diagnostic root | Twelve real Git/runtime/HTTPS cases pass | Prefix-relative CA configuration |\n| Filtered limited-provider root | 12,376 files / 327 ARM64 PEs; static closure resolves | Exact limited projections; withheld utilities excluded |\n| Coordinator's original PE gate | 327 parsed paths / 307 unique image hashes; required paths and stub checks pass | Headers and locked-file SHA only, not execution proof |\n| Independent moved consumer | Complete file readback; twelve behavior cases, SSH positive/wrong-host negative, four live ARM64/module checkpoints pass | Independent local root replay, not yet final-ZIP custody |\n| Actual console entrypoint | CMD → login Bash → Git succeeds; owned processes drain | Redirected console, not PTY/job-control certification |\n| Actual Git over native SSH | Real upload-pack, 128 KiB binary clone, second-commit fetch, exact HEAD/blob hashes and fsck; wrong-host Git clone rejected | Private encrypted loopback fixture, no installed service or real credentials |\n| Final-ZIP consumer implementation | Exact archive/manifest checks, fresh extraction, shipped-Python recreation, twelve cases, CMD launch and encrypted Git SSH replay | Ready for the final sealed ZIP; not represented as already executed on that ZIP |\n\nThe MinGW-only subset's bare-clone AV was isolated to a missing native `sh.exe` command dependency. Adding the actual native shell path made the same Git/source/configuration succeed; no gettext or Git binary rewrite was used. Original failures remain preserved.\n\n## Admission and provenance\n\n- Limited gettext admission is two original signed CLANGARM64 C DLLs plus six license files, not a GNU MINGWARM64 package alias. Default/unbound `/clangarm64` locale lookup remains unsupported; actual Git bound-domain localization is separately qualified.\n- PCRE2 retains the original unversioned `libpcre2-8.dll`; no renaming of the incompatible newer `-8-0.dll`.\n- Core utilities are a 37-command limited projection with `LC_ALL=C`, explicit MSYS system symlinks and `noacl`; no full Coreutils provider claim.\n- Microsoft ARM64 Win32-OpenSSH is a separately qualified fallback. The rejected native-MSYS SSH candidate contributes no bytes.\n- Exact published tree lookups recover missing identities for 38 already-pinned components / 7,760 payload files. Recipe identities stay labelled as recipe identities, not upstream-source/build attestations. Another 3,022 files still lack full Git commit/tree identities and retain their original package/archive/source-receipt limitations.\n- Final sealing binds 131 component provenance records, embeds 20 original producer/admission receipts, checks the exact observer inventory, independent manifest, SSH/runtime hashes and measured payload-module bytes, and preserves explicit limitations.\n\n## Remaining final gates\n\nThe published raw-exit observer preserves every Windows DWORD. Exact 7/126 cases are contracted; the distinct negative-hook Bash raw `256` remains rejected until its owner supplies the dedicated source/argv-bound contract. No blanket exit decoder, retroactive waiver or dropped hook test is used.\n\nThe pending real seal specification was exercised and correctly refused to create any output without that observer evidence. Final limited-publication scope and fresh independent **final-ZIP** custody/recreation remain outstanding. Four module checkpoints are not relabelled complete module coverage for every short-lived descendant.\n\nNo full Git for Windows release, complete native SDK/C++ qualification, Perl-dependent workflow, interactive editor/GUI/credential-service, or GSSAPI completion is claimed.","created_at":"2026-09-11T04:07:01Z","updated_at":"2026-09-11T06:11:14Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"1892c6cdca3d20de7277c120dc415876c4139bde","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/crutkas/msys2-woarm64-build/pulls/14/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/crutkas/msys2-woarm64-build/pulls/14/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/crutkas/msys2-woarm64-build/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/crutkas/msys2-woarm64-build/issues/14/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/crutkas/msys2-woarm64-build/statuses/d618c2d5d6d410b6e98b643d7262f4eb8d8072c5","head":{"label":"crutkas:crutkas-full-native-git-assembly","ref":"crutkas-full-native-git-assembly","sha":"d618c2d5d6d410b6e98b643d7262f4eb8d8072c5","user":{"login":"crutkas","id":1462282,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NjIyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1462282?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas","html_url":"https://github.com/crutkas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":true},"repo":{"id":1333319462,"node_id":"R_kgDOT3jXJg","name":"msys2-woarm64-